 ## Background
-AdpSplit was introduced in the preprint "AdpSplit: Error-Driven Adaptive Splitting for Faster Geometry Discovery in 3D Gaussian Splatting" (2026) [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the bottleneck in vanilla 3DGS where binary splitting requires many densification rounds to expose fine details, which is inefficient for accelerated training schedules [S1, unofficial]. It is integrated as a drop-in replacement for the split operator in pipelines such as 3DGS, MiniSplatting, DashGaussian, SpeedySplat, and FastGS [S1, unofficial].
+AdpSplit was introduced in the preprint "AdpSplit: Error-Driven Adaptive Splitting for Faster Geometry Discovery in 3D Gaussian Splatting" (2026) [S2, unofficial]. It addresses the bottleneck in vanilla 3DGS where binary splitting requires many densification rounds to expose fine details, which is inefficient for accelerated training schedules [S2, unofficial]. It is integrated as a drop-in replacement for the split operator in pipelines such as 3DGS, MiniSplatting, DashGaussian, SpeedySplat, and FastGS [S2, unofficial].
 
